<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Myanmar civil war (2021–present)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2021">2021</a>–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Myanmar civil war is the armed conflict that followed the military coup of February 2021, in which the army overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san-suu-kyi">Aung San Suu Kyi</a>'s elected government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-defence-force">People's Defence Forces</a> of the opposition National Unity Government and long-established ethnic armed organisations fight the junta; their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-1027">Operation 1027</a> offensive from October 2023 took large areas in the north and east of the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/myanmar-civil-war-2021-present.jpg" alt="Myanmar civil war (2021–present)" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MPATV · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mon_State_Kyomaro_Township_bombed_2024-03-28_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
